# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The four QEMU guests. NOT a .tf file: they cannot be imported with the token
# that exists, and the reason is worth more than the import.
#
# BLOCKED on a Proxmox privilege, not on a missing token (2026-09-04).
#
# `tofu plan -generate-config-out` failed on every VM with, e.g.:
#
#   error get file local-lvm:vm-102-disk-0 from datastore local-lvm:
#   403 Permission check failed (/vms/102, VM.Config.Disk)
#
# The token is `tofu@pve!import`, role PVEAuditor -- every *.Audit privilege
# and nothing else, confirmed at /access/permissions. That is enough to read
# the VM config: GET /nodes/pve/qemu/102/config returns
# `scsi0 = "local-lvm:vm-102-disk-0,iothread=1,size=15G"`, disk string included.
#
# It is the SECOND call that fails. The provider re-resolves each volume through
# GET /nodes/pve/storage/{store}/content/{volume}, and PVE gates that endpoint on
# VM.Config.Disk -- the privilege that permits *changing* disk configuration.
# So the information is readable, and the provider asks for it by a route that
# requires write authority to read.
#
# Which puts the read-only decision in GITOPS.md Phase 6 in direct conflict with
# this import. Granting VM.Config.Disk would let a token on THIS VM detach or
# resize the disks of the guests it is describing -- including
# archive-pool:vm-104-disk-0, which is the PGDATA zvol. It would NOT permit
# replacing a guest: that needs VM.Allocate, which stays withheld either way.
#
# The container in proxmox-container.tf did not hit this -- LXC volumes are read
# through a path that PVE gates on Datastore.Audit alone, which PVEAuditor has.
#
# If the decision is to grant it, on 192.168.50.101 as root:
#
#   pveum role add TofuImport -privs "VM.Audit,VM.Config.Disk,Datastore.Audit,Sys.Audit,Pool.Audit,SDN.Audit,Mapping.Audit,VM.GuestAgent.Audit"
#   pveum acl modify / --users tofu@pve --roles TofuImport
#
# ...then generate, review, confirm a clean plan, and REVOKE:
#
#   pveum acl modify / --users tofu@pve --roles PVEAuditor
#
# Generation is a one-time need. The privilege does not have to outlive it.
#
# Whatever happens, generate the bodies -- do not hand-write them. A wrong disk
# attribute on 104 does not show as a cosmetic diff; it plans a replacement, and
# that guest holds the database.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

import {
  to = proxmox_virtual_environment_vm.dev
  id = "pve/101" # 192.168.50.103 -- this dev VM, which holds this state file
}

import {
  to = proxmox_virtual_environment_vm.k3s_control
  id = "pve/102" # 192.168.50.104 -- control plane
}

import {
  to = proxmox_virtual_environment_vm.k3s_worker1
  id = "pve/103" # 192.168.50.105 -- minio
}

import {
  to = proxmox_virtual_environment_vm.k3s_worker2
  id = "pve/104" # 192.168.50.106 -- postgres; PGDATA zvol as archive-pool:vm-104-disk-0
}
